      "body": "IIUC this bug can't realistically be triggered with default `checkblocks=6` config.\r\nThis would require a `checkblocks` value of > 288 (or 0 to go all the way back) and the user would have to call `getblockfrompeer` for the block at the exact prune boundary. If a single fully-pruned block sits between the last non-pruned block and the fetched block with no undo, then this bug will not trigger.",
